1. Minimially processed as much as possible
2. All should be plant based ingredients
3. Focus on micronutrients
4. Near zero saturated fat and low fat overall, should be mostly comprised of carbs and protein since I am weight lifting
5. No artificial flavors or sweetners
6. EU compliant on all ingredients
7. 3rd party tested on all supplements
8. Most be drinkable/edible -- this means leave out anything that negatively impacts the taste. For example, for omega 3 I will do algae capsule on the side. It will not be part of the drink. I have a capsule maker so consider what spice,ingredient, or supplement would be better suited in a capsule than in the recipe
9. Focus on science backed approaches from notable plant based doctors and longevity researchers
10. No oil
11. Any supplement should have studies showing its effectiveness as an isolate
12. Try to incorporate what Bryan Johnson does with Blueprint where ever possible.
13. Ideally this would be inexpensive meal but its not necessary to sacrifice quality for lower cost
